// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 4 „Sihitis, ma-/da-infinitiiv ja rektsioon” (b1b2-016…020), stage B1+.
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline, a year after the B1 course: Sofia, who
// aims at the Tartu warehouse project (B2 module 1), gets her first big task at Tuul Logistika — the Riga furniture firm
// Silva (logistics head Ilze Berg) invites the team to a presentation. The goal, said on the first sheet: at the end the learner briefs a new colleague (Taavi) and writes him
// work instructions (019 Kasuta). Jaan's thread: the Kase kool kitchen — a new helper Pille and the kitchen rules.
// Grammar (B12H, the grammar module of the first B2 block): total vs partial object incl. the nominative object after an
// imperative and „tuleb + da” (016, again 017 and 019), ma- vs da-infinitive after verbs and „on vaja / tuleb / on
// keelatud” (017, again 019), government of verbs AND adjectives — uhke mille üle, vihane kelle peale, huvitatud
// millest, tänulik mille eest, rahul millega (018, again 019). Module 3's words (juhtuma, kogemus, viga, põhjus,
// tagajärg, aruanne, kaotama, otsima, leidma…) return in the client's story, the problem guide and the calls.
// Harno B2 formats trained in situations: semi-formal letter ~140 words (016, 018), 4-option gap text (016, 019),
// sentence-bank text (017), debate with pro/contra cards and a decision (017), a short monologue on a work topic (017,
// 018), lecture gap fill (019).
//   016 lunch at the office: what is done and what is not (listening), Ilze's letter; Markus's interim report, Jaan's
//       week in the school kitchen; Ilze's voice message — the phone call and a status letter to Ilze.
//   017 Anna's handover letter before her leave, her chat with Sofia; Jaan instructs Pille, the kitchen article, the
//       kitchen rules; Liis is ill — Riga or a video call? a debate, the decision, a letter to Liis.
//   018 Liis on the radio about volunteering; a presentation coach's article, Sofia's questions to Ilze, Kaire's
//       complaint in the kitchen; the presentation day — Ilze's advice, the talk, the questions, a thank-you letter.
//   019 the problem guide and three phone calls (Markus's passport, a late delivery, a warm fridge); Eha Org's
//       training on onboarding, Jaan's final kitchen rules, Taavi's first e-mail; Taavi's first day — the briefing
//       and the work instructions (final project).
// Lesson 5 (020) is the module's assessment in Harno form (unchanged). The v3 file is in archive/v3/b2/module04.js,
// the v1 file in archive/v1/b2/module04.js.
